===Etymology===
Two main origins:
* Borrowed from {{bor|en|de|Gau}}, a habitational surname.
* A variant of {{m|en|Gao}}, a surname of {{der|en|zh|-}} origin.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|s}}

# {{surname|en}}.

====Statistics====
* According to the 2010 United States Census, ''Gau'' is the 19703<sup>rd</sup> most common surname in the United States, belonging to 1367 individuals. ''Gau'' is most common among White (76.74%) and Asian/Pacific Islander (18.07%) individuals.

